    "check": "returned unopposed: four nominations for the ward's four seats; contests possible only in Town Hall and Harryville Wards (Ballymena Weekly Telegraph, 6 May 1949, p. 5); the Market Ward members were returned unopposed (Irish News, 20 May 1949, p. 3)",
    "url": "https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0001706/19490506/077/0005"
  },
  "note": "Borough election, 18 May 1949: twelve councillors, four for each ward (the three aldermen retired in 1952). Only the Town Hall Ward went to the poll, five candidates for four seats. The Market Ward members, four nominees for four seats, are named from the nomination report (Ballymena Weekly Telegraph, 6 May 1949, p. 5). Harryville Ward had five nominations for its four seats but was not polled; who withdrew is not found, so its members are not recorded (Irish News, 20 May 1949, p. 3). Returned unopposed."
